      "decodingStatus": "partial",
      "transforms": [
        {
          "name": "packQuantized",
          "expression": "Code = coef * (0.282095/basisScale) / max(AmbientChannel,1e-5) * 0.5 + 0.5, with basisScale 0.488603 for L1 and 1.092548/0.315392/0.546274 for L2 terms",
          "requires": [
            "AmbientRGB"
          ],
          "sourceRefs": [
            "part2.spgf.shdir.norm",
            "part2.spgf.shdir.write"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "decodeQuantized",
          "expression": "coef = (code*2 - 1) * AmbientChannel * SHDenormalizationScale, scales 0.488603/0.282095 (L1) and 1.092548/0.282095, 4*0.315392/0.282095, 2*0.546274/0.282095 (L2)",
          "requires": [
            "Code",
            "AmbientVector"
          ],
          "sourceRefs": [
            "part2.spg.usf.shdir.decode",
            "part2.spg.usf.shdir.quant"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "mathTerms": [
        "The quantization is a compile-time permutation (SH_QUANTIZE_DIRECTIONAL_COEFFICIENTS); without it the texels hold raw half coefficients and the (2*code-1) decode must NOT be applied.",
        "Six texels per probe is a channel-major layout: Red 0/1, Green 0/1, Blue 0/1, each offset by ScreenProbeAtlasViewSize.x.",
        "The six fields above all start at byte 0 of their own texel; they are not overlapping fields of a single texel. Texel (x + k*AtlasViewSize.x, y) holds channel/coefficient pair k."
      ],
      "producerSources": [
        "part2.spgf.cpp.shdir.create",
        "part2.spgf.shdir.write"
      ],
      "consumerSources": [
        "part2.spg.usf.shdir.decode"
      ],
      "gaps": [
        "Whether the stored half values are quantized codes in [0,1] or raw coefficients is decided by the SH_QUANTIZE_DIRECTIONAL_COEFFICIENTS compilation define, which is not present in the captured metadata; the two decodes give different results and neither can be selected from the texel bytes alone.",
        "The alpha channel of each half4 is unused (the 4th component is the next coefficient, not alpha)."
      ],
      "fields": [
